# public/config.js is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED.
#
# It holds the RevenueCat *publishable* key (appl_...), which ships inside every
# copy of the app, can be read out of any binary, and can neither spend money nor
# read a row of data. Ignoring it meant every build made on a machine other than
# the owner's had an empty key: purchasesAvailable() false, so the paywall said
# "in-app payment is not switched on yet", so onboarding skipped the paywall, so
# free-pick appeared alone. One missing file, three symptoms, two wasted builds.
#
# This was decided by the owner. Do not re-add an ignore rule for it.
# Real secrets - sk_live_, sb_secret_, service role, Anthropic, whsec_ - live in
# supabase secrets set and are still never committed.
